/T (The ESP32 is the central microcontroller unit of the system. It is responsible for reading all sensor data, processing it, and sending it wirelessly to the web interface. One of the key advantages of the ESP32 is its built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth capabilities, making it ideal for IoT applications. Its dual-core processor and large memory space allow for smooth multitasking and responsive real-time communication with external devices.)
/E (The ESP32 is the central microcontroller unit of the system. It is responsible for reading all sensor data, processing it, and sending it wirelessly to the web interface. One of the key advantages of the ESP32 is its built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth capabilities, making it ideal for IoT applications. Its dual-core processor and large memory space allow for smooth multitasking and responsive real-time communication with external devices.)
