/S /H2
/T (The firmware running on the ESP32 microcontroller was developed using the Arduino IDE. It handles sensor initialization, periodic reading of sensor values, and sending the data in JSON format over WebSocket to the backend server. The firmware is optimized to ensure accurate and fast communication with minimal delay, forming the core bridge between the physical environment and the digital system.)
/E (The firmware running on the ESP32 microcontroller was developed using the Arduino IDE. It handles sensor initialization, periodic reading of sensor values, and sending the data in JSON format over WebSocket to the backend server. The firmware is optimized to ensure accurate and fast communication with minimal delay, forming the core bridge between the physical environment and the digital system.)
